  [codex] EX branch correction. A recent replay-table variant exposed the same
  [codex] forwarded-operand path ending at SLTU. The current EX logic describes
  [codex] separate full-width signed and unsigned comparisons for branches, SLT,
  [codex] and SLTU, adding comparator logic and fanout after the forwarding network.
  [codex] Splitting branch resolution into another stage already lost Fmax because
  [codex] the forwarded multiply path became critical; this change keeps the stage
  [codex] boundaries and issue rate intact.
  [codex] hypothesis: |
  [codex] Compute equality and unsigned less-than once from the forwarded rs1 and
  [codex] rs2 operands using four parallel 8-bit comparisons followed by a balanced
  [codex] lexicographic combine. Derive signed less-than from operand sign bits and
  [codex] the unsigned result. Decode the branch condition as a small selection of
  [codex] equality or less-than with inversion for BNE/BGE/BGEU. Reuse the same
  [codex] segmented comparison structure for SLT and SLTU, with the ALU immediate
  [codex] operand selected separately when those instructions need it. Keep branch
  [codex] training, correction, trap checks, forwarding enables, multiply banks,
  [codex] divider, and all pipeline handshakes unchanged. The shorter comparison
  [codex] tail and reduced replicated logic should raise Gowin Fmax without changing
  [codex] CoreMark cycles; verify the new worst path, since forwarded multiplication
  [codex] is the next likely timing limit.
